00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:01.883
I like women.

00:11:01.883 --> 00:11:03.060
I've been on dates with women.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.910
I've done what I do with women and men,

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:08.970
but I'm not going to, label myself

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:11.820
just so somebody else
can put me in a category.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.560
I just always wanted to know this.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:18.270
Why is it so important that you
are identified correctly and

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.700
the, the need to come out?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.533
- Yep.

00:11:20.533 --> 00:11:23.070
- The need to say I am this. I am that.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:27.570
- Personally, I saw just
the straight side of life

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:30.330
and I wasn't feeling the
same way my friends were.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.610
And like, when you get middle
school, high school, college,

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:33.990
I felt wrong.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.280
I was gonna disappoint my family.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.870
I was gonna be looked at my whole life

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.220
as something less than.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.780
And I don't, if labels
are not important to you,

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:40.800
I think it's a personal thing.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.410
But for me, finding people
that were saying like,

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.550
this is why I feel this way.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.530
I'm like, I felt that way too.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:47.363
- When you said, well,

00:11:47.363 --> 00:11:49.194
why is it such a big deal
to come out of the closet?

00:11:49.194 --> 00:11:53.130
Like imagine being in a
closet. It's dark, it's lonely.

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:56.220
Like you don't have anyone
to express your feelings to.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.860
And I also think
representation is so important.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:11:59.693
- Yes.

00:11:59.693 --> 00:12:02.730
- Like personally, I grew
up with a mom and a dad.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.070
Then my parents split up and
now my mom is married to a

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:09.090
woman and they were actually
the first black, same sex

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:11.430
couple to be on the cover
of Essence Magazine.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.020
- [Group] Wow.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:13.853
- I know, right.

00:12:13.853 --> 00:12:15.180
Representation is so important.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.370
- What if there were no labels?

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.140
What would that look like?

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.160
- There would be no community.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.400
There would be, no, I feel
like if there were no labels,

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:24.840
it's sad to say but,

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.030
I feel like a lot of people
would be in the closet,

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.530
would be in the dark.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.380
Hi, my name is Aimee and I am a lesbian.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.600
I did hide myself for a very long time,

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.510
just because I do come from
a very strict household.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.730
I did endure, you know,

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:42.000
actually being in that hetero
relationship and actually

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.340
experiencing it firsthand.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:47.280
It took me like a whole year
of me basically ignoring him

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.650
for me to finally realize
like, I can't be doing this.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:51.660
Like, this is not who I am.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:55.039
This is not what I want
for the rest of my life.

00:12:55.039 --> 00:12:58.170
- [Announcer] I believe
traditional gender roles

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.253
are important.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.990
- Oh wait.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.210
- They're important to a degree.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.430
You know, if a man were to

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.710
date a woman and they were to get married,

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:14.610
you would expect the man to provide

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.070
and the woman to, well stay home,

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.710
or work and just raise the children.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:23.070
If we didn't have those gender norms then,

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.870
well, how would the world work?

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:28.080
- The reason I said that I
agree is 'cause the word role

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:28.980
is that word for a reason.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:30.450
A role is a performance.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.230
So it's not, we don't
need to naturalize it.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:37.530
We don't need to say women are
this one and men are this one

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:40.140
or whatever your body is,
means your destiny is this.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.130
I just think that the,

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.970
as social performances in
ways of organizing our lives,

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.550
we're not ever gonna really get rid of the

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.530
masculine feminine thing.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.170
So I think acknowledging it so
that we can think critically

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.390
about it is what matters.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.800
- I believe we're in a space

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.030
where we're starting to like,

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.180
tear down things that we are
not entirely understanding

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.220
or appreciating why it was built.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:03.570
We have to appreciate that

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.790
we have to have some type of structure.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:09.090
Now does that structure mean
that because I am born with a

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.930
certain genitalia, this is the
role I'm destined to be in?

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:17.010
I don't know. It depends on
which society you belong to.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:19.800
I don't want to do everything. I don't.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.950
That's why gender roles are important too.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:24.630
You are designating.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.520
This is what you do, this is what I do.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.750
I think that's okay.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.030
I am Marsha and I am straight.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.120
I think a lot of the decisions
that we make come from

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.320
pre-programming.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.480
For one, I'm Jamaican born.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.410
In Jamaica, being homosexual
is a no, we don't do that.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.570
There was only one way, you were straight.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:43.710
That was it.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.460
So part of my decision is
definitely my upbringing,

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:50.130
but it's also from my
experiences and realizing

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.380
this is my fit.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:53.630
This works better for me.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:01.980
- Me and my girlfriend.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.510
We don't perform gender roles, at all.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.690
Like, we care for each other
equally and it's definitely

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:10.800
a bit different, I think.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.600
- Do y'all live together?

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.433
- No.

00:15:13.433 --> 00:15:14.266
- That makes a difference too.

00:15:14.266 --> 00:15:15.120
- But we, for the past three weeks,

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.650
we've been living together though, so.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.200
- That may shift, the
longer you live together.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.033
- Yeah.

00:15:20.033 --> 00:15:21.270
- I mean, I don't see why,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:24.420
like certain household
responsibilities should be defined

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.880
by gender, especially 'cause
like I grew up with two moms,

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.400
so I never was like, oh like
this is like my mom and my dad,

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.550
like this is my mom and my mom
and both my parents worked.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.560
They like threw my ass in
daycare and it was just like

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.030
in a way, I guess I had two dads,

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.880
if you wanna like put it in that way.

00:15:38.983 --> 00:15:41.670
But like I think it's like
about a balance of like sharing

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.440
responsibility, you know?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.540
- Well, but does saying that
the gender roles are important

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.670
mean that we're saying that
they should be employed?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.760
'Cause I'm not saying that they
should be forced on anybody.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.220
- It's just whether and how
much you wanna like, take it on.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.290
- They should not be forced on everybody.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.939
But When you're talking about
doing the dishes and whatnot.

00:15:57.939 --> 00:16:01.080
My ex-husband was the
person who stayed at home.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.730
I was the one who was at work.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.763
He was the one that was
doing the dishes and cooking.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:10.353
- [Announcer] The world would
be a better place without men.

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.800
- Oh I was just like
thinking historically like,

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:20.130
men have been the one
that have caused wars

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:24.690
and created a place
where women didn't have

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:29.460
the same respect or capacity
to be heard and seen.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.450
I think it'd be easier in
a sense for me personally.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.440
I think a lot of the times
men don't understand,

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:40.500
that I could be a woman
that doesn't want to

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.760
end up with a man.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.160
That they wanna like change me or

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.290
a man and woman is like
the only right way.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.860
Hi, my name is Jayme and
I am on the lesbian side.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.320
I think it just comes down
to that I know I'm capable

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.270
of being with men and
I find them attractive

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.960
and like I could see myself
being with them sexually.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.580
But like romantically,

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.523
I don't think I could ever
really connect to a man.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.750
- With men's power, so to speak,

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.630
it gets like almost too extreme.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.520
Like, you know, look
what's happening today,

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.350
with the old white men trying to

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:18.630
control abortion or women's bodies.

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:22.860
But today, I think we would
still need them in the world

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.410
just to have at least a
different perspective.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:26.243
- Yep.

00:17:26.243 --> 00:17:27.330
- I mean, I really
struggled with this question

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.590
because looking back,

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:31.350
the only person in my
life who's ever hit me

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.020
was a fem lesbian.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.660
I have had experiences with kind of,

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.370
unwanted sexual advances
and things with men

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.480
and all of that's been bad too,

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:42.510
but like my very worst trauma
that has just stuck with me

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.470
was a woman.

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:45.930
- I don't think it'd be better
without men, but I do think

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:49.860
men need to be a little
more educated on things.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.930
Even how we're treated in school by boys.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:54.600
Like growing up was always

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.670
- If they hurt you, they like you.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.110
If they yank on your pigtails.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.270
- So I don't think we
should like abolish all men,

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:04.260
but I do think there needs
to be some leveling out.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.450
- I think that definitely
we're getting there.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:10.350
I feel like, because of what
men have done in the past,

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.300
you know, in our history,

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.720
I feel like that's why they
have this superiority again

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.700
over all of the women.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.090
But I do think that we are here

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.418
because of what we've gone through.

00:18:24.418 --> 00:18:26.797
(group applauds)

00:18:26.797 --> 00:18:29.630
(soft jazz music)

